        "intro": {
          "type": "chapter",
          "settings": {
            "title": "1. Introduction",
            "text": "<p>PB Fulfill is operated by Handel (Ningbo) Electronic Commerce Co., Ltd.</p><p> </p><p>In this Privacy Policy, “PB Fulfill,” “we,” “us,” and “our” refer to Handel (Ningbo) Electronic Commerce Co., Ltd.</p><p> </p><p>This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, store, and protect personal information when you:</p><p> </p><p>• Visit our website at pbfulfill.com;</p><p>• Submit an inquiry or request a quotation;</p><p>• Communicate with us by email, WhatsApp, online form, or another channel;</p><p>• Create an account or enter into a business relationship with us;</p><p>• Use our product sourcing, quality inspection, private-label, packaging, warehousing, fulfillment, shipping, returns, or related services; or</p><p>• Otherwise interact with PB Fulfill.</p><p> </p><p>By using our website or services, you acknowledge that you have read this Privacy Policy. Where applicable law requires consent for a specific processing activity, such as certain cookies, advertising technologies, or marketing communications, we will request that consent separately.</p>"
          }
        },
        "data_collect": {
          "type": "chapter",
          "settings": {
            "title": "2. Our Role When Processing Personal Information",
            "text": "<p>PB Fulfill primarily provides business-to-business sourcing, warehousing, fulfillment, and logistics services to ecommerce merchants and other business clients.</p><p> </p><p>When we collect personal information directly from a website visitor, prospective client, business contact, or PB Fulfill client for our own business purposes, we generally determine how and why that information is processed.</p><p> </p><p>When a business client provides us with information concerning its customers, order recipients, or other individuals so that we can fulfill orders and provide related services, we generally process that information on behalf of and according to the instructions of that business client.</p><p> </p><p>The exact legal role of PB Fulfill may depend on the circumstances, the services provided, and applicable law.</p>"
          }
        },
        "order_issue": {
          "type": "chapter",
          "settings": {
            "title": "3. Personal Information We Collect",
            "text": "<p>The information we collect depends on how you interact with us and which services you use.</p><p> </p><p>3.1 Information You Provide Directly</p><p> </p><p>We may collect information that you provide to us, including:</p><p> </p><p>• Name;</p><p>• Email address;</p><p>• Telephone or WhatsApp number;</p><p>• Company name;</p><p>• Company website or online store URL;</p><p>• Business type, sales platform, target market, and estimated order volume;</p><p>• Country, region, billing address, shipping address, and business address;</p><p>• Account registration and login information;</p><p>• Product sourcing and quotation requirements;</p><p>• Product names, links, images, specifications, quantities, and target prices;</p><p>• Sample, customization, private-label, packaging, logo, and design requirements;</p><p>• Inventory, warehousing, fulfillment, and shipping instructions;</p><p>• Order, payment, invoice, and transaction information;</p><p>• Messages, files, images, designs, logos, product documentation, and other materials that you send to us;</p><p>• Feedback, reviews, survey responses, and customer-support communications;</p><p>• Marketing and communication preferences; and</p><p>• Any other information you voluntarily provide.</p><p> </p><p>3.2 Payment and Transaction Information</p><p> </p><p>When a payment is made through our website or through a third-party payment service, payment information may be processed by Shopify, a payment processor, a bank, or another financial service provider.</p><p> </p><p>We may receive limited information such as:</p><p> </p><p>• Billing details;</p><p>• Payment status;</p><p>• Payment method type;</p><p>• Transaction reference;</p><p>• Invoice information; and</p><p>• Order or account information associated with the payment.</p><p> </p><p>We do not typically receive or store complete payment card numbers or complete bank account credentials when those details are processed directly by a third-party payment provider.</p><p> </p><p>3.3 Information Collected Automatically</p><p> </p><p>When you visit or interact with our website, we and our service providers may automatically collect technical and usage information, including:</p><p> </p><p>• Internet Protocol address;</p><p>• Approximate location derived from your IP address;</p><p>• Browser type and browser version;</p><p>• Device type, device identifiers, and operating system;</p><p>• Network and language settings;</p><p>• Referring website or source;</p><p>• Pages viewed and links clicked;</p><p>• Actions taken on the website;</p><p>• Date, time, duration, and frequency of visits;</p><p>• Campaign and referral information;</p><p>• Cookie identifiers and similar online identifiers;</p><p>• Website performance and error information; and</p><p>• Security, fraud-prevention, and diagnostic information.</p><p> </p><p>For more information about cookies and related technologies, please review our Cookie Policy.</p><p> </p><p>3.4 Information Received from Third Parties</p><p> </p><p>Where permitted by law, we may receive personal information from:</p><p> </p><p>• Shopify;</p><p>• Business clients;</p><p>• Suppliers and manufacturers;</p><p>• Warehouses and fulfillment partners;</p><p>• Shipping carriers and freight forwarders;</p><p>• Customs brokers;</p><p>• Payment processors and financial institutions;</p><p>• Analytics and advertising providers where those services are enabled;</p><p>• Communication platforms;</p><p>• Review and reputation platforms;</p><p>• Business partners and referral partners; and</p><p>• Publicly available business sources.</p>"
          }
        },
        "quality_issue": {
          "type": "chapter",
          "settings": {
            "title": "4. Information Processed on Behalf of Business Clients",
            "text": "<p></p><p> </p><p>To provide sourcing, warehousing, fulfillment, shipping, returns, and after-sales services, our business clients may provide us with information about their customers or order recipients.</p><p> </p><p>This information may include:</p><p> </p><p>• Recipient name;</p><p>• Shipping and delivery address;</p><p>• Telephone number;</p><p>• Email address;</p><p>• Order number;</p><p>• Product and quantity information;</p><p>• Delivery instructions;</p><p>• Shipment and tracking information;</p><p>• Customs or import information where required;</p><p>• Return, replacement, refund, or complaint information; and</p><p>• Other information reasonably required to process and deliver an order.</p><p> </p><p>We use this information to provide services to the relevant business client, including processing, packing, shipping, tracking, delivering, returning, replacing, or otherwise managing orders.</p><p> </p><p>The business client is generally responsible for determining how and why its customer information is collected and for providing any required privacy notices to its customers.</p><p> </p><p>If you are an end customer of one of our business clients and have a question or privacy request concerning your order, you should normally contact the merchant or online store from which you purchased the product.</p><p> </p><p>Where required, we will assist our business clients in responding to valid privacy requests.</p>"
          }
        },
        "shipping_logistics": {
          "type": "chapter",
          "settings": {
            "title": "5. How We Use Personal Information",
            "text": "<p></p><p> </p><p>We may use personal information for the following purposes:</p><p> </p><p>• To respond to inquiries and provide quotations;</p><p>• To assess product sourcing, customization, packaging, inventory, fulfillment, and shipping requirements;</p><p>• To source products and coordinate with suppliers and manufacturers;</p><p>• To arrange samples, production, quality inspections, private labeling, and packaging;</p><p>• To manage warehousing, inventory, picking, packing, fulfillment, shipping, tracking, returns, and after-sales services;</p><p>• To create and manage accounts, orders, transactions, and client relationships;</p><p>• To process payments and maintain financial records;</p><p>• To issue quotations, invoices, account statements, and payment confirmations;</p><p>• To communicate about quotations, orders, production, inventory, shipping, account activity, and customer support;</p><p>• To operate, maintain, secure, and improve our website and services;</p><p>• To understand website usage and service performance;</p><p>• To remember preferences and personalize website functionality;</p><p>• To send newsletters, company updates, educational content, service information, and promotional communications where permitted;</p><p>• To measure marketing performance where the relevant tools are enabled and where any required consent has been obtained;</p><p>• To detect and prevent fraud, abuse, security incidents, and unlawful activity;</p><p>• To protect our business, clients, users, service providers, and partners;</p><p>• To enforce our agreements and policies;</p><p>• To comply with accounting, tax, customs, trade, regulatory, legal, and record-keeping obligations; and</p><p>• To establish, exercise, or defend legal claims.</p>"
          }
        },
        "requirements": {
          "type": "chapter",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Third-Party Services & Links",
            "text": "<p>Our website may feature links to external platforms or third-party tools. They operate their services under their own privacy policies, and we are not responsible for any privacy invasion they may cause you. We recommend you reviewing their policies carefully before providing yoiur personal information.</p>"
          }
        },
